      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the probability that it will rain on both Saturday and Sunday, we need to use the fact that the probabilities are independent. The probability of an event happening and another event happening at the same time is the product of their individual probabilities. Here, the probability that it will rain on Saturday is \\(60\\%\\) and the probability that it will rain on Sunday is \\(25\\%\\).\n\nFirst, convert the percentages to decimals for calculation:\n\\[60\\% = 0.60\\]\n\\[25\\% = 0.25\\]\n\nNext, multiply these probabilities together:\n\\[0.60 \\times 0.25 = 0.15\\]\n\nNow, convert the decimal back to a percentage:\n\\[0.15 = 15\\%\\]\n\nTherefore, the probability that it will rain on both Saturday and Sunday is \\(\\boxed{15}\\).",
